    css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28, P3, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "CSS declarations inside /* */ rule-body comments leak into the cascade after a ; split", doc/08_tracking/bug/css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28.md, 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: POSTPONED per owner directive (css html fixes to postpone). The fix WAS implemented and verified in the lane tree (sb_strip_comments before ; tokenization on both rule-body parser paths; spec 6/6 PASS): style_block.spl sb_strip_comments (string/url-safe byte-slice pass), style_block_parse.spl parse_declarations strips before split, simple_web_html_layout_renderer_core_css_rules.spl extract loop strips raw rule bodies. The change was REVERTED from the landing per the directive; the bug row returns to open with this note so a future lane can reapply (design + verification evidence recorded here). Residual notes: _css_scan_rules_simple can truncate a body when a comment contains braces; inline style attributes bypass the fixed points; custom-prop harvesters scan raw bodies; dom_bridge.spl has a separate parse_declarations."
    css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 css-comment-frac lane (work/webrender-css-comment-frac-20261128): the rule scanner split a <style> sheet on { } ; without removing comments. _css_strip_comments (core_css_rules) replaces every /* */ with a space before the custom-property pre-pass and the rule scan; quote-aware ('/*' inside a string is content); a sheet without '/*' is returned untouched. Evidence: css_rule_body_comment_chrome159_spec base 0/5 -> lane 5/5 (rule-body start, mid body, inside a value, before / inside a selector, whole commented rule, quoted '/*'); Chrome 159 getBoundingClientRect values; 1x catalog lane = base; dispatch counts +0.00 %."
    css_rule_body_comment_decl_leak_2026-11-28, 2, "2026-11-28 review fix (same lane): _css_strip_comments skips a backslash-escaped quote, ends a bad string at its newline (CSS Syntax 4.3.5) and does not open a comment inside an unquoted url(...) (4.3.6). AC-6 of css_rule_body_comment_chrome159_spec (cases m..u, Chrome 159 getBoundingClientRect): lane 6/6, old stripper 5/6 (AC-6 red). The spec writes the #m and #q rules as {{ }} pieces: the plain literal lost its escapes (doc/08_tracking/bug/str_literal_brace_group_with_escaped_quote_skips_escapes_2026-11-28.md)."
